{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he passes.</b> Some say: behold, days are coming when one who passes through the land of Judah, and he is of Judah, will be hard-pressed and hungry because of the army of Sennacherib. And when he sees that neither his king nor his idol will save him, then he will look upward to pray to the God of the heavens. But in my opinion it concerns the army of Sennacherib, which will pass through the land of Judah — and it is known that a large camp hungers." "<b>In his king.</b> It is the king of Assyria." "And when he looks upward and downward, he will see everything as darkness."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:54.624765611Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}